{"ref":"BDB, גָּלְיַת","hw":"גָּלְיַת","html":"† <big><span dir=\"rtl\">גָּלְיַת</span></big>  <strong>n.pr.m. (</strong><em>conspicuous</em>? On ending ת cf. Dr <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 17:4\" href=\"/I_Samuel.17.4\">1 S 17:4</a> & Nö in Eut<sup>Nab 73</sup><strong>)</strong> (<span dir=\"rtl\">גָּלְיָת</span> <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 20:5\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.20.5\">1 Ch 20:5</a>) Philistine giant slain by David <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 17:4\" href=\"/I_Samuel.17.4\">1 S 17:4</a>, <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 17:23\" href=\"/I_Samuel.17.23\">23</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 21:10\" href=\"/I_Samuel.21.10\">21:10</a>; <a data-ref=\"I Samuel 22:10\" href=\"/I_Samuel.22.10\">22:10</a>, but according to <a data-ref=\"II Samuel 21:19\" href=\"/II_Samuel.21.19\">2 S 21:19</a> slain by Elhanan of Bethlehem (<span dir=\"rtl\">בֵּית הַלַּחְמִי</span>; according to <a data-ref=\"I Chronicles 20:5\" href=\"/I_Chronicles.20.5\">1 Ch 20:5</a> Elhanan slew <span dir=\"rtl\">לַחְמִי</span> brother of Goliath).","next":"BDB, יָגְלִי","prev":"BDB, גִּלָּיוֹן"}